  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1) \nSome light rain is possible east of I-75 this morning. Low stratus\ndeck will linger through the morning hours today, but drier mid level\nair will begin to advect into the region and gradually dissolve some\nof the clouds this afternoon. This will result in the beginning of a\nprolonged stretch of drier weather.\n\nSynoptically, the Ohio Valley remains on the western periphery of an\nupper level trough, which is driving the cooler/cloudier pattern. We\nwill begin to see a large cut off low develop along the Atlantic \nCoast, creating a blocking pattern through the weekend. This will \nresult in a fairly stagnant weather pattern through the next several \ndays, with a constant advection of some drier air out of the NE. \nThus, a much needed stretch of drier weather conditions are expected,\nalong with temperatures that will trend below seasonal normals.",
